      "description": "The single next step of a view, Action Blue fill.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn ds-btn-primary\">Start Part 1 <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/></svg></button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn{min-height:48px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);background:var(--surface);border-radius:10px;padding:0 18px;font:600 16px Onest,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;color:var(--ink);transition:background .12s;cursor:pointer}.ds-btn svg{width:18px;height:18px}.ds-btn-primary{background:var(--act);border-color:var(--act);color:var(--on-act)}.ds-btn-primary:hover{background:color-mix(in oklab,var(--act) 88%,var(--ink))}.ds-btn:active{transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-btn:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--act);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Secondary Button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-secondary",
      "description": "Every other action; white with a strong hairline.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn2\">Check with coach</button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn2{min-height:48px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);background:var(--surface);border-radius:10px;padding:0 18px;font:600 16px Onest,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);transition:background .12s;cursor:pointer}.ds-btn2:hover{background:var(--sunken)}.ds-btn2:active{transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-btn2:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--act);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Filter Chips",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "chip-filter-selected",
      "description": "Pill filters; the selected one is Board Navy.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-chips\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\">All</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Part 1</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Part 2</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Part 3</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-chips{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-family:Onest,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-chips button{min-height:38px;padding:0 14px;border-radius:999px;font:500 14px inherit;font-family:inherit;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer}.ds-chips button:hover{background:var(--sunken)}.ds-chips button[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--board);border-color:var(--board);color:var(--on-board);font-weight:600}.ds-chips button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--act);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Test-date Chip",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "exam-chip",
      "description": "Header chip with the test date; amber when unset.",
      "html": "<div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px\"><button class=\"ds-exam\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4\"/></svg>Test Sat 12 Dec · 26 days</button><button class=\"ds-exam ds-exam-unset\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4\"/></svg>Set test date</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-exam{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:5px 11px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--sunken);font:600 14px Onest,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);border:0;min-height:32px;cursor:pointer}.ds-exam svg{width:16px;height:16px}.ds-exam-unset{background:var(--signal-soft);color:var(--signal-ink)}.ds-exam:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--act);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Part Badges",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "part-badge",
      "description": "22px numeral badges in the three part colours.",
      "html": "<div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px\"><span class=\"ds-badge\">1</span><span class=\"ds-badge ds-p2\">2</span><span class=\"ds-badge ds-p3\">3</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-badge{display:inline-grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:5px;color:var(--on-part);font:700 13px Onest,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;line-height:1;background:var(--p1)}.ds-p2{background:var(--p2)}.ds-p3{background:var(--p3)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Length Zone Bar",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "",
      "description": "Part 1 zones: short to 20 s, target 20-30 s, over to 45 s; blue fill grows while speaking.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-zonewrap\"><div class=\"ds-timer\">0:24</div><div class=\"ds-zone\"><span class=\"z1\"></span><span class=\"z2\"></span><span class=\"z3\"></span><i style=\"width:53%\"></i></div><div class=\"ds-zlab\"><span>0 s</span><span class=\"g\">20–30 s</span><span>45 s</span></div><div class=\"ds-zstate\">Good length</div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-zonewrap{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;font-family:Onest,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:360px}.ds-timer{font-size:56px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ink)}.ds-zone{position:relative;height:12px;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;display:grid;gap:2px;grid-template-columns:20fr 10fr 15fr}.ds-zone .z1{background:var(--warn-soft)}.ds-zone .z2{background:var(--ok-soft)}.ds-zone .z3{background:var(--sunken)}.ds-zone i{position:absolute;left:0;top:0;bottom:0;background:var(--act);border-radius:6px 0 0 6px;transition:width .25s linear}.ds-zlab{display:grid;grid-template-columns:20fr 10fr 15fr;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted)}.ds-zlab .g{color:var(--ok);font-weight:600}.ds-zlab span:last-child{text-align:right}.ds-zstate{font-size:15px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ok)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Record Dock",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "record-button",
      "description": "Bottom dock while recording: soft red, 2px red edge, pulsing stop button.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-dock\"><button class=\"ds-dbtn\">Skip</button><div class=\"ds-mid\"><button class=\"ds-rec\" aria-label=\"Stop\"><span></span></button><span class=\"ds-lbl\">Recording</span></div><span></span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-dock{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:12px 18px;min-height:96px;background:var(--rec-soft);border-top:2px solid var(--rec);font-family:Onest,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-mid{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:4px}.ds-rec{width:76px;height:76px;border-radius:50%;border:0;background:var(--rec);display:grid;place-items:center;box-shadow:0 4px 14px color-mix(in oklab,var(--rec) 32%,transparent);animation:dspulse 1.4s ease-in-out infinite;cursor:pointer}.ds-rec span{width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:5px;background:var(--on-rec)}.ds-rec:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--act);outline-offset:2px}@keyframes dspulse{50%{box-shadow:0 0 0 10px color-mix(in oklab,var(--rec) 18%,transparent)}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-rec{animation:none}}.ds-lbl{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--rec-ink)}.ds-dbtn{justify-self:start;min-height:48px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);background:var(--surface);border-radius:10px;padding:0 14px;font:600 16px inherit;font-family:inherit;color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer}.ds-dbtn:hover{background:var(--sunken)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "List Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card",
      "description": "Hairline list in a 14px card; rows 56px with part badge and chevron.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-list\"><a class=\"ds-li\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-b\">1</span><span class=\"ds-g\"><span class=\"t\">Do you work or study?</span><span class=\"s\">2 answers · 0:27</span></span><span class=\"ds-chev\">&rsaquo;</span></a><a class=\"ds-li\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-b ds-b3\">3</span><span class=\"ds-g\"><span class=\"t\">Why do people move to cities?</span><span class=\"s\">Not answered yet</span></span><span class=\"ds-chev\">&rsaquo;</span></a></div>",
      "css": ".ds-list{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;font-family:Onest,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:480px}.ds-li{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:12px 14px;min-height:56px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--ink);text-decoration:none}.ds-li:first-child{border-top:0}.ds-li:hover{background:var(--sunken)}.ds-li:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--act);outline-offset:-2px}.ds-li .t{display:block;font-weight:600}.ds-li .s{display:block;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.ds-g{flex:1;min-width:0}.ds-chev{color:var(--line-strong);font-size:22px}.ds-b{display:inline-grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:5px;background:var(--p1);color:var(--on-part);font-weight:700;font-size:13px;flex:none}.ds-b3{background:var(--p3)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Text Input",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input",
      "description": "White field, strong hairline, blue border and 3px ring on focus.",
      "html": "<input class=\"ds-input\" type=\"search\" placeholder=\"Search words\">",
      "css": ".ds-input{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:10px;padding:10px 12px;min-height:44px;width:100%;max-width:360px;font:400 16px Onest,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink)}.ds-input::placeholder{color:var(--muted)}.ds-input:focus{border-color:var(--act);outline:none;box-shadow:0 0 0 3px color-mix(in oklab,var(--act) 22%,transparent)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Bottom Tabs",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "",
      "description": "Four tabs; active tab is navy with a 3px navy bar on top (left edge on the 96px rail).",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-tabs\"><a aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M3 11l9-7 9 7v9H3z\"/></svg><span>Today</span></a><a href=\"#\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M9.5 9.5a2.5 2.5 0 1 1 3.5 2.3c-.6.3-1 .9-1 1.6M12 17h.01\"/></svg><span>Questions</span></a><a href=\"#\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"3\" width=\"6\" height=\"11\" rx=\"3\"/><path d=\"M5 11a7 7 0 0 0 14 0M12 18v3\"/></svg><span>My answers</span></a><a href=\"#\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M4 5h7a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v12a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H4zM20 5h-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2\"/></svg><span>Words</span></a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-tabs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);height:64px;max-width:420px;background:var(--surface);border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-family:Onest,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-tabs a{position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:3px;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none}.ds-tabs a:hover{color:var(--ink)}.ds-tabs a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--act);outline-offset:-2px}.ds-tabs svg{width:22px;height:22px}.ds-tabs a[aria-current=page]{color:var(--board);font-weight:700}.ds-tabs a[aria-current=page]::before{content:'';position:absolute;top:0;left:30%;right:30%;height:3px;border-radius:0 0 3px 3px;background:var(--board)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Test Room",
    "overview": "A white, calm room with one job in it: say the next answer out loud. The page is plain white and pale blue-grey; colour is spent on meaning, never on decoration. Each strong colour has exactly one job (blue acts, navy marks where you are, amber marks what is next, red means the microphone is on), so a user can read the state of the screen from colour alone. The only constant chrome is a white header carrying the test-date chip, because the date is the reason the app exists.\n\nDensity is moderate and phone-first: one column, 44px touch targets, a bottom tab bar of four (Today / Questions / My answers / Words) with settings behind a gear. On a computer (900px and up) the same components stay the same size; the tab bar becomes a 96px left rail and pages split into a main column and a side column. Nothing grows into a dashboard.\n\nProgress is shown as plain measured facts (seconds spoken, pauses, band estimates from the coach) and never as a game. There are no streaks, points, badges, confetti or daily targets. The coach costs a request and runs only when the user presses its button.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White header and surfaces on a cool off-white page (hue 262 throughout the neutrals).",
      "One family, Onest variable, for everything, including timers.",
      "Colour by job: act blue, board navy, signal amber, record red, three part colours.",
      "Part identity carried by 22px numeral badges, not by tinted screens.",
      "A length-zone bar per part is the main piece of feedback while speaking.",
      "Flat surfaces with 1px hairlines; shadows only on things that float.",
      "Full light and dark themes from the same token names."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Job Per Colour Rule",
        "body": "Blue acts, navy marks the current place or selection, amber marks what is next or unset, red means recording. Never borrow one colour for another job; a primary button is never navy, a selected chip is never blue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Means Live Rule",
        "body": "Record red appears only on the record control, the live-recording dock and header line, and the level meter. Destructive text buttons use `rec-ink` as text only, with no red fill.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Ambers Rule",
        "body": "`signal` (bright, yellow-amber) is \"next / due / unset\". `warn` (dark, brown-amber) is \"too short / check this\". They do not swap.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Proportional Digits Rule",
        "body": "Body text sets `proportional-nums`. Only ticking timers and counters (`tabular-nums`) get fixed-width digits, so they do not jitter while counting.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight Not Size Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy comes from weight steps between 500 and 700 and a short size range (12.5px to 30px); the only large type is a running timer.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Only Floaters Cast Shadows Rule",
        "body": "Cards, lists and buttons never carry a shadow. If it does not sit above the page (sheet, modal, toast, record button), it is flat.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the header white and put the test-date chip in it on every main screen; switch it to the amber \"Set test date\" state when the date is missing.",
      "Do use Action Blue for the single primary button of a view, and Board Navy only for the active tab marker, the selected chip or pill, and the current item.",
      "Do label every question with its 22px part badge in teal (1), orange (2) or violet (3).",
      "Do show the length zone bar for the question's part while recording, with the ranges Part 1 20-30 s, Part 2 90-120 s, Part 3 45-60 s.",
      "Do report progress as measured facts (seconds, pauses, band estimates) in plain sentences.",
      "Do use `tabular-nums` on ticking timers and counters only.",
      "Do keep touch targets at 44px and reuse the same components on phone and computer; only the shell (tabs to 96px rail) and column count change.",
      "Do honour `prefers-reduced-motion`: the build turns off all animation and transitions under it."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use red for anything except the record control, the live recording state and the level meter.",
      "Don't use Signal Amber for warnings or Warn amber for \"next\"; the two ambers have separate jobs.",
      "Don't add game mechanics: no streaks, points, badges, confetti, celebratory copy or daily targets.",
      "Don't run the coach automatically; it runs only when the user presses \"Check with coach\".",
      "Don't put shadows on cards, lists or buttons.",
      "Don't tint whole screens or cards with a part colour; part colour lives on the badge.",
      "Don't add a second typeface; timers and labels are Onest too.",
      "Don't add small uppercase labels or kickers above headings; the \"Start here\" line on the first-run Today card is a known exception in the build, not a pattern."
    ]
  }
}